  "notes": "Kanji variant of はかる. Use {計|はか}る for measuring time or intervals, or in set phrases meaning 'to plan / to scheme'. Distinguished from {測|はか}る (physical measurement of length, depth), {量|はか}る (weight, volume), and {図|はか}る (to attempt / plan an undertaking).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {時間|じかん}を{計|はか}る: to time something\n- タイムを{計|はか}る: to measure a time\n- {解決|かいけつ}を{計|はか}る: to seek a resolution\n- {暗殺|あんさつ}を{計|はか}る: to plot an assassination\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {測|はか}る: to measure length, height, depth, speed\n- {量|はか}る: to measure weight or volume\n- {図|はか}る: to attempt or plan (large undertaking)",
